ons:\\n[Button: Compare Top Travel Cards] https://www.bankrate.com/credit-cards/travel/\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000036\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary\\nThe Herman Miller Aeron is a classic mesh task chair focused on suspended support, while the Steelcase Gesture is designed for modern tech users, supporting a wide range of postures and device-usage styles.\\n\\nErgonomic Feature Comparison\\n\\nLumbar Support\\n- Aeron (Size B): Features the PostureFit SL system. It uses two adjustable pads that stabilize the sacrum and support the lumbar region of the spine to mimic a standing posture.\\n- Gesture: Features \\\"3D LiveBack\\\" technology. The backrest automatically contours to mimic the natural movement of the spine, providing continuous support as you change positions.\\n\\nArmrest Movement\\n- Aeron (Size B): 3D Armrests. They adjust for height, depth (sliding forward/backward), and pivot (turning inward/outward). They are attached to the seat back.\\n- Gesture: 4D Armrests. Known for the best range in the industry, they adjust for height, width, depth, and 360-degree pivot. They are designed to support users holding mobile devices or tablets.\\n\\nTilt Options\\n- Aeron (Size B): Standard model includes a Tilt Limiter with three settings (upright, mid-recline, full recline) and a Seat Angle adjustment (Forward Tilt) for engaged tasks.\\n- Gesture: Features a variable back stop with four positions. It lacks the forward tilt option found on the Aeron but offers a more seamless \\\"synchro-tilt\\\" that keeps feet flat on the floor while reclining.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: View Aeron] https://www.hermanmiller.com/products/seating/office-chairs/aeron-chairs/\\n[Button: View Gesture] https://www.steelcase.com/products/office-chairs/gesture/\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://www.hermanmiller.com/content/dam/hermanmiller/documents/user_guides/Aeron_Chairs_adjustment_guide.pdf\\n- https://www.steelcase.com/content/uploads/2015/01/Gesture-Hangtag-User-Gui