very hex adjacent to your second settlement.\\n\\nResource Production\\n- Rolling Dice: On your turn, roll two 6-sided dice. The sum determines which hexes produce resources.\\n- Collecting: Any player with a settlement adjacent to a hex labeled with that number receives 1 resource card of that hex's type (Forest=Lumber, Hills=Brick, Pasture=Wool, Fields=Grain, Mountains=Ore).\\n- Cities: If you have a city on a producing hex, you receive 2 resource cards instead of 1.\\n- The Robber: If a 7 is rolled, no resources are produced. The player who rolled the 7 moves the Robber to a hex, stealing a card from an adjacent player and blocking that hex's production.\\n\\nWays to Earn Victory Points (VP)\\n1. Building: Each Settlement is worth 1 VP. Each City is worth 2 VP.\\n2. Special Cards: Development Cards can sometimes be 'Victory Point' cards worth 1 VP each (kept hidden until the end).\\n3. Achievements: \\n- Longest Road: The first player to build a continuous road of 5 or more segments gets 2 VP. \\n- Largest Army: The first player to play 3 Knight cards gets 2 VP.\\n\\nWinning: The first player to reach 10 Victory Points on their turn wins.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Hexagon: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/hexagon.png\\n- Trophy: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/trophy.png\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://www.catan.com/understand-catan/game-rules\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000087\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Lord of the Rings Extended Edition Marathon Schedule\\n\\nDate: 2025-01-10\\nLocation: New York City\\n\\nAssumptions: Runtimes used are The Fellowship of the Ring (208 min), The Two Towers (235 min), and The Return of the King (263 min).\\n\\nSchedule\\n\\n- 09:00 AM - 12:28 PM: Film 1 - The Fellowship of the Ring\\n- 12:28 PM - 12:48 PM: Break (20 minutes)\\n- 12:48 PM - 04:43 PM: Film 2 - The Two Towers\\n- 04:43 PM - 05:28 PM: Lunch/Dinner Break (45 minutes)\\n- 05:28 PM - 09:51 PM: Film 3 - The Return of the King\\n\\nTotal End Time: 09:51 PM\\n\\nMarathon Stats\\n