ret: Before the trick starts, peek at the bottom card of the deck (the 'key card'). When you cut the deck, your key card will end up directly on top of their selected card. Fan through the cards; their card is the one immediately to the right of your key card.\\n\\nTrick 2: The Upside Down Card\\nThe Setup: Before starting, turn the bottom card of the deck face up.\\nThe Performance: Hold the deck so the face-down side is up. Ask a spectator to pick a card. While they look at it, secretly flip the entire deck over in your hand. Have them slide their card back into the middle of the (now face-up) deck. Flip the deck back over behind your back or under the table.\\nThe Secret: Because you flipped the deck, their card is now the only one facing the opposite direction. Spread the cards to reveal their choice.\\n\\nTrick 3: The Spelling Bee\\nThe Setup: Place any 9 cards on the table in three rows of three.\\nThe Performance: Ask someone to think of a card in the grid. Pick up the piles so their pile is in the middle of the other two. Spell the name of a random card (e.g., Q-U-E-E-N) while dealing cards. \\nThe Secret: This is a self-working mathematical trick. If you always place their chosen pile in the middle and deal the cards in a specific sequence (3-3-3), the chosen card will always end up in the 5th position of the 9-card stack.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Magic: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/magic-wand.png\\n- Cards: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/playing-cards.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000090\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Writing Prompts: The Great Dragon City\\n\\nSetting: 'Dracopolis' - A sprawling metropolis built within the fossilized ribcage and skull of a dragon the size of a mountain.\\n\\n1. The Merchant (Archetype: Merchant)\\nYou trade in 'Dragon-Marrow Essence,' a rare fuel harvested from the deepest, most dangerous parts of the tail-districts. A rival guild has just discovered a way to synthesize it, threatening your family's legacy and the city