o the different characters? Is there a sense of moral judgment or God in this world?\\n5. Nick as Narrator: Nick Carraway claims to be 'one of the few honest people' he has ever known. Do you find him to be a reliable narrator, or does his fascination with Gatsby bias his perspective of the events?\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Toronto Public Library] https://www.torontopubliclibrary.ca\\n[Button: Discussion Guide PDF] https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/291185/the-great-gatsby-by-f-scott-fitzgerald/9780743273565/readers-guide/\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000093\",\n    \"response_text\": \"The Circle of Fifths: Music Theory Guide\\n\\nConcept\\nThe Circle of Fifths is a visual representation of the 12 tones of the chromatic scale, their corresponding key signatures, and the relationships between them. Moving clockwise, each note is a perfect fifth above the previous one (e.g., C to G).\\n\\nDetermining Key Signatures\\n- The top of the circle is C Major (no sharps or flats).\\n- Clockwise (Sharps): Each step adds a sharp. G has 1 (#F), D has 2 (#F, #C), A has 3.\\n- Counter-Clockwise (Flats): Each step adds a flat. F has 1 (Bb), Bb has 2 (Bb, Eb).\\n\\nGuitar Application: Finding Chords That Sound Good\\n1. The Neighborhood Rule: In any given key, the chords immediately to the left and right of your 'home' chord on the circle will always sound good together. For example, if you are in the key of C, the chords F (left) and G (right) are the IV and V chords, the most common companions.\\n2. Finding Relative Minors: The inner ring of the circle shows the relative minor for each major key. For C Major, it is A Minor. These two keys share the same notes and can be used interchangeably to create different moods.\\n3. The 1-4-5 Progression: Most rock and blues songs use the I, IV, and V chords. You can find them instantly: Pick a note (I), the one to the left is (IV), and the one to the right is (V).\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Music Theory: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/music-notation.png\\n- Guitar: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/acoustic-guitar.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000094\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Hamilton: Musical Summary\\n\\nAct 1: The Revolution\\nSummary: Follows Alexander Hamilton's arrival in New York, his involvement in the American Revolution, and his marriage to Eliza Schuyler.\\n- Plot Point 1: Hamilton meets Aaron Burr and his future comrades (Laurens, Lafayette, Mulligan), joining the patriot cause.\\n- Plot Point 2: Hamilton becomes George Washington's aide-de-camp and proves his brilliance at the Battle of Yorktown.\\n- Plot Point 3: The war ends, and Hamilton begins his career as a lawyer and co-author of the Federalist Papers.\\n- Key Musical Numbers: 'Alexander Hamilton', 'My Shot'.\\n\\nAct 2: The Republic\\nSummary: Focuses on Hamilton's tenure as Secretary of the Treasury, his personal scandals, and his eventual downfall.\\n- Plot Point 1: Hamilton clashes with Thomas Jefferson and James Madison over the national financial system.\\n- Plot Point 2: Hamilton's reputation is ruined by the Reynolds Affair and the death of his son, Philip, in a duel.\\n- Plot Point 3: The escalating tension with Aaron Burr culminates in a final duel in Weehawken, resulting in Hamilton's death.\\n- Key Musical Numbers: 'The Room Where It Happens', 'It's Quiet Uptown'.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Theater: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/theater-curtains.png\\n- History: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/parchment.png\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Listen on Spotify] https://open.spotify.com/album/1k8uQAs02s978Jh4Scl90s\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000095\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Steam Indie Game Budget Analysis\\n\\nGame List & Prices (Hypothetical Sale)\\n\\n- Hollow Knight: $7.50\\n- Stardew Valley: $10.00\\n- Hades: $12.50\\n- Celeste: $5.00\\n- Outer Wilds: $15.00\\n\\nTotal Cost Calculation\\n7.50 + 10.00 + 12.50 + 5.00 + 15.00 = $50.00\\n\\nBudget Remaining\\n- Starting Budget: $100.00\\n- Total Spent: