nd root vegetables.\\n\\nASSUMPTIONS\\n- Chuck steak is trimmed of excess fat and cut into 3cm cubes.\\n- A standard 5-6 quart slow cooker is used.\\n\\nINGREDIENTS\\n- 1kg Beef Chuck Steak\\n- 500g Potatoes (Yukon Gold or Red), cubed\\n- 3 Large Carrots, sliced\\n- 1 Large Onion, chopped\\n- 3 cloves Garlic, minced\\n- 250ml Dry Red Wine (Cabernet or Merlot)\\n- 500ml Beef Broth\\n- 2 tbsp Tomato Paste\\n- 1 tsp Dried Thyme\\n- 2 Bay Leaves\\n- 2 tbsp Cornstarch (for thickening)\\n- Salt and Pepper to taste\\n\\nCOOKING SETTINGS\\n- Low Setting: 8 hours (Recommended for best texture)\\n- High Setting: 4 hours\\n\\nINSTRUCTIONS\\n1. Sear (Optional but Recommended): Brown the beef cubes in a skillet with a little oil before adding to the slow cooker.\\n2. Layer: Place potatoes, carrots, and onions in the bottom of the slow cooker. Top with the beef.\\n3. Liquid: Mix beef broth, wine, tomato paste, garlic, and thyme. Pour over the beef and vegetables. Add bay leaves.\\n4. Cook: Set to Low for 8 hours or High for 4 hours.\\n5. Thicken: 30 minutes before serving, whisk 2 tbsp cornstarch with 3 tbsp cold water to create a slurry. Stir the slurry into the stew. Turn to High (if not already) and cook until the sauce thickens and becomes glossy.\\n\\nQUICK ACTIONS\\n[Button: Best Red Wines for Cooking] https://example.com/cooking-wine\\n[Button: Side Dish Suggestions] https://example.com/stew-sides\\n\\nICONS\\n- Slow Cooker: https://example.com/icons/crockpot.png\\n- Meat: https://example.com/icons/beef.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000329\",\n    \"response_text\": \"SUMMARY\\nAuthentic Thai Green Curry starts with a hand-pounded paste to release essential oils, followed by a quick simmer with coconut milk and aromatics.\\n\\nPART 1: GREEN CURRY PASTE (Mortar and Pestle)\\nIngredients:\\n- 10-15 Green Bird's Eye Chilies\\n- 2 tbsp Chopped Shallots\\n- 1 tbsp Chopped Garlic\\n- 1 tbsp Chopped Galangal\\n- 1 tbsp Sliced Lemongrass (white part only)\\n- 1 tsp Sliced Kaffir Lime Peel\\n- 1 tsp Chopped Coriander Root\\n- 1 tsp Toasted Cumin Seeds\\n- 1 tsp Toasted Coriander Seeds\\n- 1 tsp Shrimp Paste (Gapi)\\n- 1/2 tsp Salt\\nProcess: Pound the dry seeds first. Add chilies and salt, pound to a paste. Add fibrous ingredients (lemongrass, galangal, lime peel) one by one, pounding until smooth. Finish with shallots, garlic, and shrimp paste.\\n\\nPART 2: MAIN DISH (Serves 3)\\nIngredients:\\n- 500g Chicken Breast, thinly sliced\\n- 200g Bamboo Shoots (canned/sliced)\\n- 400ml Coconut Milk (Full fat)\\n- 2 tbsp Green Curry Paste\\n- 1 tbsp Palm Sugar\\n- 1.5 tbsp Fish Sauce\\n- 5-6 Thai Basil Leaves\\n- 2 Kaffir Lime Leaves, torn\\n- 1 Red Chili, sliced (for garnish)\\n\\nINSTRUCTIONS\\n1. Fry Paste: Heat 100ml of coconut milk in a wok until it starts to separate (oil beads appear). Add 2 tbsp paste and fry until fragrant.\\n2. Cook Chicken: Add chicken slices. Stir-fry until the outside is no longer raw.\\n3. Simmer: Add the rest of the coconut milk and bamboo shoots. Bring to a gentle simmer.\\n4. Season: Add fish sauce and palm sugar. Adjust to balance salty, sweet, and spicy.\\n5. Finish: Stir in Kaffir lime leaves and Thai basil. Remove from heat immediately.\\n\\nQUICK ACTIONS\\n[Button: Find Thai Ingredients] https://example.com/thai-pantry\\n[Button: Mortar vs Blender Guide] https://example.com/curry-technique\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000330\",\n    \"response_text\": \"SUMMARY\\nA nutritious, budget-friendly meal for a family of six using pantry staples. This recipe creates a savory black bean stew served over fluffy white rice.\\n\\nASSUMPTIONS\\n- Pantry spices include Salt, Pepper, Cumin, and Garlic Powder.\\n- Cooking oil and water are available.\\n- Prices are based on average US grocery store bulk pricing.\\n\\nCOST ESTIMATE (EXAMPLE)\\n- 500g Black Beans: $1.50\\n- 1kg White Rice: $2.00\\n- 2 Large Onions: $1.50\\n- 1 Can Crushed Tomatoes: $1.50\\n- Total: $6.50 (Well under the $15 budget)\\n\\nINGREDIE