nd root vegetables.\\n\\nASSUMPTIONS\\n- Chuck steak is trimmed of excess fat and cut into 3cm cubes.\\n- A standard 5-6 quart slow cooker is used.\\n\\nINGREDIENTS\\n- 1kg Beef Chuck Steak\\n- 500g Potatoes (Yukon Gold or Red), cubed\\n- 3 Large Carrots, sliced\\n- 1 Large Onion, chopped\\n- 3 cloves Garlic, minced\\n- 250ml Dry Red Wine (Cabernet or Merlot)\\n- 500ml Beef Broth\\n- 2 tbsp Tomato Paste\\n- 1 tsp Dried Thyme\\n- 2 Bay Leaves\\n- 2 tbsp Cornstarch (for thickening)\\n- Salt and Pepper to taste\\n\\nCOOKING SETTINGS\\n- Low Setting: 8 hours (Recommended for best texture)\\n- High Setting: 4 hours\\n\\nINSTRUCTIONS\\n1. Sear (Optional but Recommended): Brown the beef cubes in a skillet with a little oil before adding to the slow cooker.\\n2. Layer: Place potatoes, carrots, and onions in the bottom of the slow cooker. Top with the beef.\\n3. Liquid: Mix beef broth, wine, tomato paste, garlic, and thyme. Pour over the beef and vegetables. Add bay leaves.\\n4. Cook: Set to Low for 8 hours or High for 4 hours.\\n5. Thicken: 30 minutes before serving, whisk 2 tbsp cornstarch with 3 tbsp cold water to create a slurry. Stir the slurry into the stew. Turn to High (if not already) and cook until the sauce thickens and becomes glossy.\\n\\nQUICK ACTIONS\\n[Button: Best Red Wines for Cooking] https://example.com/cooking-wine\\n[Button: Side Dish Suggestions] https://example.com/stew-sides\\n\\nICONS\\n- Slow Cooker: https://example.com/icons/crockpot.png\\n- Meat: https://example.com/icons/beef.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000329\",\n    \"response_text\": \"SUMMARY\\nAuthentic Thai Green Curry starts with a hand-pounded paste to release essential oils, followed by a quick simmer with coconut milk and aromatics.\\n\\nPART 1: GREEN CURRY PASTE (Mortar and Pestle)\\nIngredients:\\n- 10-15 Green Bird's Eye Chilies\\n- 2 tbsp Chopped Shallots\\n- 1 tbsp Chopped Garlic\\n- 1 tbsp Chopped Galangal\\n- 1 tbsp Sliced Lemongrass (white part only)\\n- 1 tsp Slice