: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/000000/bright-moon.png\\n- Tripod: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/000000/tripod.png\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://www.visitnorway.com/things-to-do/nature-highlights/northern-lights/how-to-photograph-the-northern-lights/\\n- https://digital-photography-school.com/step-by-step-guide-to-photographing-the-northern-lights/\"\n  },\n  {\n", "raw": {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "[\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000641\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: This 5-day itinerary focuses on the vibrant anime culture, cutting-edge technology, and family-friendly museums of Tokyo, specifically tailored for children aged 8 and 10.\\n\\nAssumptions: Family is staying in a central location like Shinjuku or Shibuya. Travel is via the Tokyo subway system.\\n\\n5-Day Itinerary:\\n\\nDay 1: Akihabara (The Electric Town)\\n- Morning: Explore the multi-story Radio Kaikan for anime merchandise.\\n- Afternoon: Visit a themed cafe (e.g., Square Enix Cafe) and the Gigo Arcade.\\n- Evening: Experience the neon lights and interactive electronics stores.\\n- Neighborhood: Akihabara\\n\\nDay 2: Odaiba (Tech and Fun)\\n- Morning: Miraikan (National Museum of Emerging Science and Innovation) for robotics.\\n- Afternoon: teamLab Planets for an immersive digital art experience.\\n- Evening: See the life-sized Unicorn Gundam Statue.\\n- Neighborhood: Odaiba\\n\\nDay 3: Mitaka and Kichijoji (Studio Ghibli)\\n- Morning: Ghibli Museum (requires booking months in advance).\\n- Afternoon: Inokashira Park and the Ghibli-themed shops.\\n- Evening: Explore the kid-friendly atmosphere of Kichijoji.\\n- Neighborhood: Mitaka / Kichijoji\\n\\nDay 4: Ueno (Culture and Science)\\n- Morning: National Museum of Nature and Science (interactive dinosaur and tech exhibits).\\n- Afternoon: Ueno Zoo or the Tokyo National Museum.\\n- Evening: Ameya Yokocho market for snacks.\\n- Neighborhood: Ueno\\n\\nDay 5: Shibuya and Harajuku (Modern Trends)\\n- Morning: Nintendo TOKYO and