{"prompt_hash": "c823ae2f9035737923204ec750f39c051d42d90fca52dcb94de36e2676a255dd", "text": "[\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000561\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Assumptions: Nutritional values are based on 100g of cooked grain.\\n\\nSummary\\nQuinoa is a nutritionally dense seed often categorized as a whole grain. It offers significantly higher protein and fiber than brown rice and has a lower glycemic impact.\\n\\nNutritional Comparison Table\\nMetric | Cooked Quinoa | Cooked Brown Rice\\nProtein | 4.4g | 2.6g\\nFiber | 2.8g | 1.8g\\nGlycemic Index | 53 (Low) | 68 (Medium)\\nCalories | 120 kcal | 111 kcal\\n\\nKey Differences\\n- Protein Quality: Quinoa is a complete protein containing all nine essential amino acids. Brown rice is incomplete.\\n- Satiety: The higher fiber and protein in quinoa generally lead to increased fullness.\\n- Blood Sugar: Quinoa's lower GI makes it a better choice for blood sugar management.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Nutrition: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/healthy-food.png\\n- Health: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/heart-monitor.png\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Quinoa Recipes] https://www.allrecipes.com/search?q=quinoa\\n[Button: Brown Rice Recipes] https://www.allrecipes.com/search?q=brown+rice\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000562\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary\\nCard A provides a higher net value due to its consistent cashback rate across all spending and the absence of an annual fee, despite Card B's higher rewards in specific categories.\\n\\nCalculations\\nMonthly Spend: $500 (Dining) + $200 (Travel) + $1,300 (Other) = $2,000 total.\\n\\nCard A (2% Flat Rate):\\n- Monthly Rewards: $2,000 * 0.02 = $40\\n- Annual Rewards: $40 * 12 = $480\\n- Annual Fee: $0\\n- Net Annual Value: $480\\n\\nCard B (4% Dining/Travel, 1% Other):\\n- Monthly Dining/Travel: $700 * 0.04 = $28\\n- Monthly Other: $1,300 * 0.01 = $13\\n- Total Monthly Rewards: $41\\n- Annual Rewards: $41 * 12 = $492\\n- Annual Fee: $95\\n- Net Annual Value: $492 - $95 = $397\\n\\nComparison Table\\nMetric | Card A | Card B\\nGross Annual Rewards | $480 | $492\\nAnnual Fee | $0 | $95\\nNet Annual Value | $480 | $397\\n\\nRecommendation\\nChoose Card A. It results in $83 more profit per year based on your spending habits.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Finance: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/money-box.png\\n- Credit Card: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/credit-card.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000563\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary\\nThe Tesla Model 3 Long Range excels in acceleration and charging network integration, while the Hyundai Ioniq 6 Limited offers faster peak charging speeds and a unique aerodynamic design.\\n\\nTechnical Specifications Table\\nFeature | 2023 Tesla Model 3 LR | 2023 Hyundai Ioniq 6 Limited\\nEPA Estimated Range | 333 miles | 270 miles\\n0-60 mph Acceleration | 4.2 seconds | 5.1 seconds\\nMax DC Fast Charge Rate | 250 kW | 350 kW\\nCharging Time (10-80%) | ~27 minutes | ~18 minutes\\nDrivetrain | All-Wheel Drive | All-Wheel Drive\\n\\nKey Considerations\\n- Efficiency: The Ioniq 6's 800V architecture allows for faster charging at compatible 350kW stations.\\n- Performance: Tesla maintains a significant lead in raw acceleration and software integration.\\n- Range: Tesla offers more range, though Ioniq 6 range varies significantly by wheel size (the Limited trim has 20-inch wheels).\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Electric Car: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/electric-car.png\\n- Charging: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/charging-station.png\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Tesla Configurator] https://www.tesla.com/model3/design\\n[Button: Hyundai Ioniq 6 Info] https://www.hyundaiusa.com/us/en/vehicles/ioniq-6\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000564\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Assumptions: Weather data reflects historical averages for October.\\n\\nSummary\\nOctober is a prime shoulder-season month for both cities. Kyoto offers vibrant autumn foliage and mild humidity, while Florence provides crisp Mediterranean air and fewe