_text\": \"Troubleshooting Guide: Model X200 Printer\\nSymptoms: Flashing paper jam light, no visible paper, grinding noise.\\n\\nStep 1: Check Rear Duplexer\\n- Power off the printer and unplug the power cord.\\n- Turn the printer around and locate the rear access panel or duplexer.\\n- Press the release buttons to remove the duplexer module.\\n- Inspect for small scraps of paper or debris caught in the rollers.\\n- Reinsert the duplexer until it clicks into place.\\n\\nStep 2: Clear Internal Path\\n- Open the main cartridge access door.\\n- Gently slide the print head carriage from side to side to ensure no obstructions are causing the grinding noise.\\n- Use compressed air to clear dust from the internal sensors.\\n\\nStep 3: Reset the Paper Sensor\\n- With the printer still unplugged, press and hold the Power button for 15 seconds to drain residual energy.\\n- Plug the printer back in and power it on.\\n- If the light still flashes, perform a hard reset: while on, unplug the cord from the back, wait 30 seconds, and reconnect.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Download Manual] https://support.printercorp.com/x200/manual\\n[Button: Contact Support] https://support.printercorp.com/contact\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Warning: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/000000/warning.png\\n- Maintenance: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/000000/settings.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000764\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Daily Medication Schedule\\nPatient: Anonymous\\n\\nMedication | Dosage | Timing | Purpose | Taken [X]\\nLisinopril | 10mg | Once daily (Morning) | Blood Pressure | [ ]\\nMetformin | 500mg | Twice daily (With Breakfast) | Blood Sugar | [ ]\\nMetformin | 500mg | Twice daily (With Dinner) | Blood Sugar | [ ]\\nAtorvastatin | 20mg | Once daily (Before Bed) | Cholesterol | [ ]\\n\\nInstructions\\n- Take Metformin specifically during or immediately after meals to reduce stomach upset.\\n- Consistency is key; try to take your morning and evening doses at the same time each day