on: Check the box for Waiting Room. This ensures participants cannot join until the host admits them.\\n- Options Section: Click Show. Check the box for Mute participants upon entry.\\n- Save the meeting.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Open Zoom Web Portal] https://zoom.us/signin\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://support.zoom.com/hc/en/article?id=zm_kb&sysparm_article=KB0063467\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000420\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: AWS S3 offers various storage classes optimized for different access patterns, costs, and retrieval times.\\n\\nComparison Table:\\nStorage Class | Durability | Minimum Storage Duration | Retrieval Time\\nS3 Standard | 99.999999999% | None | Milliseconds\\nS3 Intelligent-Tiering | 99.999999999% | 30 Days | Milliseconds\\nS3 Glacier Instant Retrieval | 99.999999999% | 90 Days | Milliseconds\\nS3 Glacier Deep Archive | 99.999999999% | 180 Days | 12-48 Hours\\n\\nKey Recommendations:\\n- Use S3 Standard for active data with frequent access.\\n- Use S3 Intelligent-Tiering if access patterns are unknown or changing.\\n- Use S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval for rare access but immediate needs.\\n- Use S3 Glacier Deep Archive for long-term compliance backups (1-2 times a year access).\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Cloud Storage: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/cloud-storage.png\\n- Database: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/database.png\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://aws.amazon.com/s3/storage-classes/\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000421\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Database templates in Notion allow you to pre-fill properties and content for every new page created within that database.\\n\\nSteps to Create the Template:\\n1. Open your Notion database.\\n2. Click the blue arrow next to the New button in the top right corner.\\n3. Select + New template.\\n4. Title the template (e.g., New Task Template).\\n\\nConfiguring Automatic Properties:\\n- Status: Click the Status property field and select To Do from the dropdown.\\n- Priority: Click the Priority property field (assuming it is a Select/Multi-select type) and choose your default level (e.g., Medium).\\n- Created Date: You do not need to set this in the template. Instead, ensure your database has a property of the type Created time. This is a system-generated property that automatically logs the date and time for every new entry.\\n\\nFinalizing:\\n- Exit the template editor. \\n- To make this the default, click the blue arrow next to New again, click the three dots (...) next to your template name, and select Set as default for all views.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Notion Help Center] https://www.notion.so/help/guides/using-database-templates\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000422\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: A clean installation removes all existing data and provides a fresh operating system environment on your new NVMe SSD.\\n\\nPreparation:\\n- A USB drive with at least 8GB of space.\\n- A working PC to create the media.\\n\\n10-Step Installation Guide:\\n1. Download the Windows 11 Media Creation Tool from Microsoft.\\n2. Run the tool and select Create installation media for another PC; choose your USB drive.\\n3. Insert the USB drive and the new NVMe SSD into the target PC.\\n4. Power on the PC and tap the Boot Menu key (usually F12, F11, F10, or F8) repeatedly.\\n5. Select the USB Flash Drive as the primary boot device.\\n6. Select your language and keyboard preferences, then click Install Now.\\n7. Select I don't have a product key (you can activate later via your Microsoft account).\\n8. Choose Custom: Install Windows only (advanced).\\n9. Select the Unallocated Space on your NVMe SSD and click Next. Windows will automatically partition the drive.\\n10. Follow the on-screen OOBE (Out of Box Experience) to set up your region, account, and privacy settings until you reach the desktop.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Download Windows 11 Media] https://www.microsoft.com/software-download/windows11\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/create-installation-media-for-windows-99a58364-8c02-206f-aa6f-40c3b507420d\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000423\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: This function uses the filter method to isolate items in the specific category and the reduce method to calculate the sum.\\n\\nJavaScript Code:\\n\\nfunction getTotalElectronicsPrice(inventory) {\\n  return inventory\\n    .filter(item => item.category === 'Electronics')\\n    .reduce((accumulator, currentItem) => accumulator + currentItem.price, 0);\\n}\\n\\nExample Usage:\\n\\nconst items = [\\n  { name: 'Laptop', price: 1200, category: 'Electronics' },\\n  { name: 'Phone', price: 800, category: 'Electronics' },\\n  { name: 'Desk', price: 150, category: 'Furniture' }\\n];\\n\\nconst total = getTotalElectronicsPrice(items);\\nconsole.log(total); // Output: 2000\\n\\nLogic Explanation:\\n- .filter(): Creates a new array containing only objects where the category property is exactly 'Electronics'.\\n- .reduce(): Iterates through the filtered array, adding each item's price to a running total (accumulator) starting at 0.\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/reduce\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000424\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Faint vertical lines are usually caused by dust on the corona wire or a worn-out drum unit surface.\\n\\nHow to Clean the Primary Corona Wire:\\n1. Open the front cover of the printer and leave it open for 10 minutes to let it cool down.\\n2. Remove the drum unit and toner cartridge assembly.\\n3. Locate the green tab on top of the drum unit.\\n4. Gently slide the green tab from left to right and right to left several times.\\n5. Important: Return the green tab to the Home position (marked by an arrow/triangle). Failure to do so causes a thick black vertical stripe.\\n6. Reinstall the assembly and close the cover.\\n\\nIdentifying if the Drum Needs Replacement:\\n- Drum Life Warning: The printer will display a Replace Drum or Drum Near End message on the LCD or through the status monitor.\\n- Physical Damage: If cleaning the corona wire does not fix the lines, inspect the surface of the black roller on the drum unit. Any scratches, nicks, or toner buildup that matches the position of the lines on the paper indicates the drum is physically damaged.\\n- Page Count: The DR730 drum unit is typically rated for approximately 12,000 pages.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Brother Support Manual] https://support.brother.com/g/b/producttop.aspx?c=us&lang=en&prod=hll2350dw_us\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://help.brother-usa.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/154868\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000425\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Setting a static IP ensures your computer always uses the same address on your local network, which is useful for hosting services or remote access.\\n\\nConfiguration Steps:\\n1. Press the Windows Key + I to open Settings.\\n2. Go to Network & Internet.\\n3. Click on Ethernet (or Wi-Fi, depending on your connection).\\n4. Click on your active connection name.\\n5. Scroll down to IP settings and click Edit.\\n6. Change the setting from Automatic (DHCP) to Manual.\\n7. Toggle the IPv4 switch to On.\\n\\nEnter the following parameters:\\n- IP Address: 192.168.1.50\\n- Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.0\\n- Default Gateway: 192.168.1.1\\n- Preferred DNS: 8.8.8.8\\n- Alternate DNS: 8.8.4.4 (Optional but recommended)\\n\\n8. Click Save to apply the changes.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- Open Command Prompt and type ipconfig to verify the settings are active.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Network: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/network.png\\n- Settings: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/settings.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000426\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: This Dockerfile creates a lightweight, production-ready container for a Node.js application using the Alpine Linux distribution.\\n\\nDockerfile Content:\\n\\n# Use the specific base image\\nFROM node:18-alpine\\n\\n# Set the working directory inside the container\\nWORKDIR /app\\n\\n# Copy package files first to leverage Docker cache for dependencies\\nCOPY package*.json ./\\n\\n# Install production dependencies\\nRUN npm install --production\\n\\n# Copy the rest of the application code\\nCOPY . .\\n\\n# Expose the port the app runs on\\nEXPOSE 3000\\n\\n# Command to run the application\\nCMD [\\\"node\\\", \\\"index.js\\\"]\\n\\nInstructions:\\n1. Save the code above as a file named Dockerfile in your project root.\\n2. Build the image: docker build -t my-node-app .\\n3. Run the container: docker run -p 3000:3000 my-node-app\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://docs.docker.com/language/nodejs/containerize/\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000427\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Power Query is a powerful data transformation tool in Excel that can handle large datasets like your 10,000-row CSV efficiently.\\n\\nSteps to Clean Your Data:\\n1. Import Data: Go to the Data tab in Excel, click Get Data > From File > From Text/CSV. Select your file and click Import.\\n2. Open Editor: In the preview window, click Transform Data to open the Power Query Editor.\\n3. Remove Duplicates: \\n   - Locate the CustomerID column.\\n   - Right-click the column header.\\n   - Select Remove Duplicates. This ensures every CustomerID is unique.\\n4. Filter Purchase Amount:\\n   - Locate the PurchaseAmount column.\\n   - Click the drop-down arrow in the column header.\\n   - Select Number Filters > Greater Than.\\n   - Enter 500 in the box and click OK.\\n5. Load Data: Click Close & Load in the top left corner to return the cleaned data to a new Excel worksheet.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Power Query Documentation] https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/about-power-query-in-excel-71047ec7-9512-42b7-af3d-272514c97444\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000428\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Adding an M.2 SSD to your PS5 significantly increases storage capacity for PS5 and PS4 games.\\n\\nSSD Requirements:\\n- Interface: PCIe Gen4 x4 M.2 NVMe SSD\\n- Capacity: 250GB - 8TB\\n- Read Speed: 5,500MB/s or faster recommended\\n- Form Factor: 2230, 2242, 2260, 2280, or 22110\\n- Heatsink: Required (either built-in or added manually)\\n- Max Width: 25mm\\n\\nTools Needed:\\n- A #1 Phillips head screwdriver\\n- A flat, stable work surface with a soft cloth\\n\\nInstallation Steps:\\n1. Power off the PS5, unplug all cables, and let it cool down.\\n2. Remove the base. Place the console with the PS logo facing down and the power button facing away from you.\\n3. Gently lift the back corner of the cover and slide it toward the base to remove it.\\n4. Remove the screw from the expansion slot cover and remove the cover.\\n5. Remove the screw and spacer from the 110 mark. Move the spacer to the mark corresponding to your SSD size (usually 80).\\n6. Insert the SSD into the connector at an angle until it clicks, then secure it with the screw over the spacer.\\n7. Reattach the expansion slot cover and the PS5 outer cover.\\n8. Reconnect cables and power on.\\n\\nFormatting:\\n- Upon boot, a M.2 SSD Storage guide will appear. Select Format M.2 SSD. The console will run a speed test and confirm the drive is ready for use.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Hardware: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/memory-slot.png\\n- Gaming: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/playstation.png\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://www.playstation.com/en-us/support/hardware/ps5-install-m2-ssd/\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000429\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Choosing a VPN protocol involves balancing speed, security, and device efficiency. WireGuard is currently the industry leader for modern performance.\\n\\nTechnical Comparison:\\n\\nProtocol | Encryption Strength | Connection Speed | Battery Consumption\\nWireGuard | ChaCha20 (Modern/Fast) | Very High | Low (Most Efficient)\\nOpenVPN | AES-256 (Industry Std) | Moderate/High | High (Heavy Load)\\nIKEv2 | AES-256 (Robust) | High | Moderate (Mobile Optimized)\\n\\nKey Insights:\\n- WireGuard: Best for almost all use cases. It has a much smaller code base (approx. 4,000 lines), making it faster to audit and extremely quick to connect.\\n- OpenVPN: Best for compatibility and bypassing strict firewalls (TCP mode). It is highly configurable but can be slower on mobile devices.\\n- IKEv2: Best for mobile users who frequently switch between Wi-Fi and Cellular data, as it excels at re-establishing lost connections quickly.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Security: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/shield.png\\n- Speed: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/speed.png\\n- Battery: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/battery.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000430\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: The 'Error Establishing a Database Connection' typically means WordPress cannot communicate with your MySQL database due to incorrect credentials or a server failure.\\n\\nTroubleshooting Flowchart:\\n\\n1. Verify wp-config.php Credentials\\n   - Access your site via FTP/SFTP or File Manager.\\n   - Open wp-config.php and check these four lines:\\n     DB_NAME (Database Name)\\n     DB_USER (Username)\\n     DB_PASSWORD (Password)\\n     DB_HOST (Usually 'localhost', but sometimes an IP provided by the host)\\n\\n2. Test Database Connection with a Script\\n   - Create a file named testdb.php in your root directory with a simple PHP mysqli_connect script. If it fails, the credentials in Step 1 are definitely wrong.\\n\\n3. Check MySQL Service Status\\n   - If you have access to the server (VPS/Dedicated), run: service mysql status or service mariadb status.\\n   - If it is stopped, run: sudo service mysql start.\\n\\n4. Repair the Database\\n   - Add define('WP_ALLOW_REPAIR', true); to your wp-config.php file.\\n   - Visit: yoursite.com/wp-admin/maint/repair.php.\\n\\n5. Contact Hosting Provider\\n   - If steps 1-4 fail, the database server may be down or your account may have hit its resource limits.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: WordPress Debugging Guide] https://wordpress.org/documentation/article/debugging-in-wordpress/\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000431\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: The bug in your code is the use of a mutable default argument (items=[]). In Python, default arguments are evaluated only once at the time of function definition, not every time the function is called.\\n\\nWhy it is problematic:\\n- When you call add_item('A'), it works as expected. \\n- However, if you call add_item('B') without providing a list, it will use the same list object that now contains 'A'. \\n- This causes the list to persist and grow across different function calls, which is usually unintended behavior.\\n\\nCorrected Version:\\n\\ndef add_item(name, items=None):\\n    if items is None:\\n        items = []\\n    items.append(name)\\n    return items\\n\\nExplanation of the fix:\\n- By setting the default to None (an immutable type), you ensure that a new list is created inside the function scope every time the function is called without an explicit list argument.\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://docs.python-guide.org/writing/gotchas/#mutable-default-arguments\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000432\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: To ensure accurate outdoor run tracking, your Apple Watch relies on a combination of its own hardware and GPS data from your paired iPhone.\\n\\nRequired iPhone Settings:\\n1. Location Services: Go to Settings > Privacy & Security > Location Services. Ensure it is toggled On.\\n2. Apple Watch Workout: In the list of apps under Location Services, find Apple Watch Workout and set it to While Using the App.\\n3. System Services: Scroll to the bottom of the Location Services page and tap System Services. Ensure Motion Calibration & Distance is toggled On.\\n\\nCalibration Steps:\\n- Wear your Apple Watch and go to a flat, open outdoor area with good GPS reception.\\n- Open the Workout app on your watch.\\n- Start an Outdoor Walk or Outdoor Run.\\n- Walk or run at your normal pace for about 20 minutes.\\n- This process calibrates the accelerometer by learning your stride length at different speeds, improving accuracy when GPS is unavailable or weak.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- GPS: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/marker.png\\n- Fitness: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/5", "raw": {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "[\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000418\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Enabling Developer Options and USB Debugging allows for advanced system modifications and communication between your phone and a computer.\\n\\nAssumptions: You are using the default Samsung One UI 6.0/6.1 interface on Android 14.\\n\\nStep 1: Enable Developer Options\\n- Open the Settings app.\\n- Scroll to the bottom and tap About phone.\\n- Tap Software information.\\n- Find Build number and tap it rapidly seven times. You will see a toast notification saying Developer mode has been turned on.\\n\\nStep 2: Enable USB Debugging\\n- Go back to the main Settings menu.\\n- Scroll to the very bottom; a new entry called Developer options will now appear below About phone.\\n- Tap Developer options.\\n- Scroll down to the Debugging section.\\n- Toggle the switch for USB debugging to the On position.\\n- Tap OK when the confirmation prompt appears.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Settings: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/settings.png\\n- Developer: https://img.icons8.com/ios-filled/50/code.png\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Samsung Support Guide] https://www.samsung.com/us/support/answer/ANS00087642/\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://developer.android.com/studio/debug/dev-options\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000419\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary: Configuring a recurring meeting in Zoom ensures the same Meeting ID and settings are reused for every session.\\n\\nConfiguration Steps:\\n1. Sign in to the Zoom Web Portal or Desktop Client.\\n2. Click Meetings and then Schedule a Me