ord).\\n- Label: The account name (e.g., 'MyBank:user@email.com').\\n- Secret: A Base32 encoded string (the private key used to generate codes).\\n- Issuer: The name of the service (e.g., 'Google', 'GitHub').\\n- Algorithm: Usually SHA1 (default).\\n- Digits: Number of digits in the code (usually 6).\\n- Period: Time interval for new codes (usually 30 seconds).\\n\\nSources:\\n- https://github.com/google/google-authenticator/wiki/Key-Uri-Format\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000863\",\n    \"response_text\": \"UI Mockup: Smart Home Onboarding\\n\\nScreen Layout:\\n- Top: 'Adding New Device' header.\\n- Center: Square scanning viewfinder. (User points this at the light bulb base).\\n- Overlay: Once a code is detected, the viewfinder blurs.\\n- Bottom Section: Progress indicator.\\n  - Status: Pairing with Hub...\\n  - Progress Bar: [||||||||||----------] 50%\\n  - Hint: 'Keep your phone close to the Smart Bulb'.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Cancel Pairing] action://setup/cancel\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000864\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Donation QR Template (SMS)\\n\\nRaw String for QR Code:\\nSMSTO:70707:GIVE10\\n\\nUser Experience:\\n1. User scans the code.\\n2. Phone prompts: 'Send SMS to 70707?'\\n3. SMS app opens with '70707' in the 'To' field and 'GIVE10' in the message body.\\n4. User presses 'Send' to complete the donation.\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Open SMS] sms:70707?body=GIVE10\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000865\",\n    \"response_text\": \"QR Code vs. Data Matrix\\n\\nPreferred Industry:\\nData Matrix is the standard in the Aerospace, Automotive, and Medical Device industries.\\n\\nWhy Data Matrix is Preferred:\\n- Size: Data Matrix can be significantly smaller than QR codes (down to 2-3mm square) while still holding 50+ characters.\\n- Marking Requirements: It is optimized for 'Direct Part Marking' (DPM), such as laser etching or dot-peening onto metal or plastic surfaces.\\n- Reliability: It has higher readability on low-