{"prompt_hash": "4b53c28e3f334dfd8097d1e80a50dfb58e2a0cc48305b2d6ae37c2dbd6906f3c", "text": "[\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000452\",\n    \"response_text\": \"SYSTEM OVERVIEW\\nIn the world of Aethelgard, magic is not cast through incantations but through the raw channeling of the user's psyche. This is known as the Resonance. Practitioners must physically manifest the feeling to trigger the corresponding elemental or physical shift.\\n\\nEMOTIONAL SPECTRUM AND EFFECTS\\n\\n1. RAGE (Pyrokinesis)\\nEffect: Generates intense heat and combustion. The intensity of the flame scales with the user's level of fury, often resulting in blue flames for pure, cold rage or explosive bursts for volatile anger.\\n\\n2. SERENITY (Cryokinesis and Stasis)\\nEffect: Freezes moisture in the air and slows the kinetic energy of surrounding objects. A calm mind can create intricate ice structures or halt a projectile in mid-air.\\n\\n3. GRIEF (Gravitational Distortion)\\nEffect: Increases the weight of objects or the user themselves. Deep sorrow creates a 'heavy' atmosphere where enemies find it difficult to move or even breathe under the crushing pressure.\\n\\n4. JOY (Aerokinesis and Levitation)\\nEffect: Manipulates air currents and reduces the effect of gravity. Pure elation allows for flight, swift movement, and the creation of protective gale-force winds.\\n\\n5. TERROR (Illusion and Phasing)\\nEffect: Distorts the perception of others and allows the user to become 'ghost-like' or intangible. Fear causes the user to slip between the cracks of reality to avoid harm.\\n\\nTHE MAJOR COST: EMOTIONAL EROSION\\nThe 'Price of the Pulse' is the permanent loss of the emotion used. Frequent channeling of Rage eventually leaves the mage incapable of feeling anger, resulting in a state of permanent apathy. Once an emotion is 'burned out,' the corresponding magic is lost forever, leaving the practitioner a hollow shell known as a 'Gray-Soul.'\\n\\nQUICK ACTIONS\\n[Button: View World Map] https:/