oth)\\n- [ ] 1 Tablespoon of Crushed Bone Dust (Sea Salt)\\n- [ ] 1 Teaspoon of Dried Bat Wings (Black Peppercorns)\\n- [ ] Garnish: Ghostly Essence (Sour Cream or Coconut Milk for swirls)\\n\\nINSTRUCTIONS\\n1. Sauté the Mandrake Root and Vampire Repellent in a large cauldron (pot) with a splash of oil until translucent.\\n2. Toss in the cubed Dragon's Hearts and stir to coat in the essence.\\n3. Pour in the Swamp Water until the ingredients are fully submerged. Bring to a rolling boil.\\n4. Reduce heat and simmer for 20 minutes or until the Dragon's Hearts are tender.\\n5. Stir in the Beetle Husks and cook for another 5 minutes.\\n6. Use an immersion wand (blender) to liquefy the brew until smooth and dark.\\n7. Serve in bowls with a swirl of Ghostly Essence to create a spiderweb pattern on top.\\n\\nQUICK ACTIONS\\n[Button: Print Recipe] https://spooky-eats.com/witchs-brew/print\\n[Button: Shop Ingredients] https://grocery-delivery.com/halloween-list\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000462\",\n    \"response_text\": \"PLOT OUTLINE: MURDER ON THE ORIENT EXPRESSWAY (1935)\\n\\nSETTING\\nThe luxury 'Star of the East' locomotive traveling from Paris to Istanbul. A heavy snowstorm traps the train in the Balkan mountains.\\n\\nTHE VICTIM\\nLord Alistair Sterling: A ruthless antiquities dealer known for stealing cultural artifacts. Found dead in the locked First Class Smoking Carriage.\\n\\nTHE WEAPON\\nA decorative silver letter opener belonging to the train's conductor, found wiped clean of fingerprints but coated in a rare, fast-acting venom from the Amazon.\\n\\nTHE SUSPECTS\\n1. Countess Elena Volkov: A Russian exile whose family jewels were 'purchased' by Sterling for a fraction of their worth. Motive: Revenge and financial restoration.\\n2. Dr. Aris Thorne: A disgraced archaeologist whose career Sterling ruined after Thorne refused to authenticate a forgery. Motive: Professional spite.\\n3. Julianna 'Jules' Vance: A professional lounge singer. It is revealed s