r). No salary raises or stock price changes are calculated.\\n\\nTotal Compensation Comparison\\nOffer | Year 1 Total | Year 4 Total\\nOffer 1: £60k + 10% Bonus | £66,000 | £66,000\\nOffer 2: £65k Flat | £65,000 | £65,000\\nOffer 3: £55k + Stock | £57,500 | £57,500\\n\\nSummary\\n- Offer 1 is the strongest financially in both the short and long term, provided the 10% bonus is achieved.\\n- Offer 2 provides the highest guaranteed base pay without relying on performance or vesting.\\n- Offer 3 has the lowest total value, as the stock options do not bridge the gap created by the lower base salary.\\n\\nRecommendation\\nChoose Offer 1 for maximum total earnings. Choose Offer 2 if you prefer a guaranteed monthly cash flow without bonus risk.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Career: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/job-seeker.png\\n- Money: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/stack-of-money.png\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query_id\": \"q_000568\",\n    \"response_text\": \"Summary\\nFor high-heat searing (such as steaks or stir-fry), Avocado Oil is the best choice due to its exceptionally high smoke point and healthy fat profile.\\n\\nProperties Comparison Table\\nOil/Fat | Smoke Point | Primary Fat Type | Best Use\\nAvocado Oil | 520 F (270 C) | Monounsaturated | High-heat searing/frying\\nExtra Virgin Olive Oil | 375 F (190 C) | Monounsaturated | Dressings, low-heat saute\\nGhee (Clarified Butter) | 485 F (250 C) | Saturated | Searing, Indian cuisine\\n\\nDetailed Analysis\\n- Avocado Oil: Highest smoke point; very stable and neutral flavor.\\n- Extra Virgin Olive Oil: Lower smoke point; heat can destroy delicate flavors and beneficial compounds.\\n- Ghee: High smoke point and rich buttery flavor; contains more saturated fat than the plant oils.\\n\\nRecommendation\\nUse Avocado Oil for temperatures above 500 F. Use Ghee if you want a high smoke point with a rich, savory flavor profile.\\n\\nIcons:\\n- Cooking: https://img.icons8.com/color/48/cooking-pot.png\\n- Health: https://img.icons8.com/color/