epresentation of the 12 tones of the chromatic scale, their corresponding key signatures, and the relationships between them. Moving clockwise, each note is a perfect fifth above the previous one (e.g., C to G).\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"key-sig-card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"key-sig-col\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"key-sig-col\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"key-sig-title\",\n            \"key-sig-body\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"key-sig-title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Determining Key Signatures\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"key-sig-body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"- **Top:** C Major (no sharps or flats).\\n- **Clockwise (Sharps):** Each step adds a sharp. G has 1 (#F), D has 2 (#F, #C), A has 3.\\n- **Counter-Clockwise (Flats):** Each step adds a flat. F has 1 (Bb), Bb has 2 (Bb, Eb).\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"guitar-section-col\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"guitar-header-row\",\n            \"guitar-tabs\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"guitar-header-row\",\n          \"component\": \"Row\",\n          \"align\": \"center\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"guitar-icon\",\n            \"guitar-title\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"guitar-icon\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": \"/acoustic-guitar.png\",\n          \"variant\": \"icon\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"guitar-title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Guitar Application\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"guitar-tabs\",\n        